The "PAUSED" menu overflows after 25 level loads (the crash after many loads and restarts)

Every level load, restarts included (Progress::RestartScene reloads the level), runs Game_ReloadLevel, which builds the
two pause menus: the pause menu and the one-item "PAUSED" menu (g_pausedMenu). Game_FreeLevel empties the pause menu's
nodes before the next load, but nothing empties the "PAUSED" menu's: PausedMenu_ClearItems (0x5465fd) is never called.
So every load appends two more nodes (a page and its item) to g_pausedMenu, whose array g_pausedMenuItems (0x6de9c0)
holds 50 and whose add functions never check that. From the 26th load since the game was started, each load writes 16
bytes past the array's end, a little further every time, over whatever comes next in memory:

  loads 26-40   the pause menu's four slider cursors (g_menuCursors 0x6deb58)
  loads 41-44   the pause box and text rectangles and the progress snapshot (0x6dec48-0x6dec83)
  load  45      g_pauseResumeIndex, g_pauseRebinding and the pause menu's exit / restart request flags (0x6dec84-0x6dec8f)
  loads 46-67   the message box: its text, rectangle and frame (0x6dec90-0x6dedef)
  loads 68-92   the pause menu's own nodes (g_pauseMenuItems 0x6dedf8), just after they are built for that level
  load  93      g_pMenuNoiseTexture (0x6def88): the same load then reads through it (Menu_CreateNoiseTexture, from
                Menus_LoadLevelUi), and the value written there is two node fields, not a Texture
  loads 95-99   g_quitPending and the list heap's allocator state (g_listNodeHeap 0x6defa8)
  load  99      g_scratch32k (0x6defe8), the 32 KB block the next level free releases

Most of the rest is rewritten later in the same load or when the pause menu opens, so the damage shows where a value
stays wrong: the pause menu's own nodes (a crash or a broken menu when Start is pressed, loads 68-92) and the noise
texture pointer (most likely a crash during the 93rd load; if the address written there happens to be readable, the
load can survive and a later one crashes). Only the Start press depends on the player, which is why the count of
loads before a crash varies. Every full load counts: the first scene at start-up, the studio, levels, restarts, and the
attract demos. This is read from the code; not yet seen in the running game (g_pausedMenu.count, the s16 at
0x57c158, should read twice the number of loads since the game started).

This fix empties the "PAUSED" menu in Game_FreeLevel, next to the pause menu.

Touches: src/engine/game_level.cpp (Game_FreeLevel).

diff --git a/src/engine/game_level.cpp b/src/engine/game_level.cpp
index 2bed064..0571809 100644
